Hi @{{ author }}, thank you for the report.

This issue looks like a model download problem. 

The MFlux-Community can only support official upstream models (eg black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-9b-kv), as well as the [MFlux-Community models on HuggingFace](https://huggingface.co/mflux-community). 

We find that many model problems are due to corrupt or missing models files. 

**Please try;**
```
hf cache verify --fail-on-missing-files {hugging-face/model_path}
```


To retry the model download use; 
```
hf download {hugging-face/model_path}
```


If the issue was not a corrupt model please confirm that you have;

1. Updates MFlux to the latest release.
2. Have enough enough free space on your disk.
3. If the model is gated on Hugging Face (for example FLUX.1-dev), accept the license on the model page. Then log in: `hf auth login`.

If the same error occurs after a clean download, please reply with:

- The full command(s) you ran.
- The full error output.
- The macOS version and the amount of RAM.

We will then look at the issue. This comment was posted by an automated triage action. A maintainer will review the issue if the steps above do not help.
